1
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:10,461
How can fifty million pounds of extra investment
create two hundred million pounds of extra
income?

2
00:00:10,471 --> 00:00:13,879
The income expenditure diagram shows how.

3
00:00:14,788 --> 00:00:18,781
National income and output are on the horizontal
axis.

4
00:00:18,791 --> 00:00:22,623
Planned aggregate expenditure is on the vertical
axis.

5
00:00:22,633 --> 00:00:27,225
Both axes measure millions of pounds, using
equal scales.

6
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:33,948
Assume a closed economy without government,
fixed prices, and enough spare capacity.

7
00:00:33,958 --> 00:00:37,856
Households consume seventy five percent of
income.

8
00:00:37,866 --> 00:00:42,458
Initially, planned investment is one hundred
million pounds.

9
00:00:43,364 --> 00:00:47,488
Planned expenditure equals consumption plus
investment.

10
00:00:47,498 --> 00:00:51,383
The line starts at one hundred on the vertical
axis.

11
00:00:51,393 --> 00:00:56,985
Its slope is the marginal propensity to consume:
zero point seven five.

12
00:00:57,892 --> 00:01:03,437
The forty five degree line shows every point
where planned expenditure equals output.

13
00:01:03,447 --> 00:01:05,793
It is a reference line.

14
00:01:05,803 --> 00:01:10,079
Equilibrium occurs where the planned expenditure
line crosses it.

15
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:15,709
Initially, equilibrium income is four hundred
million pounds.

16
00:01:15,719 --> 00:01:20,881
Consumption is three hundred million, and
investment is one hundred million.

17
00:01:20,891 --> 00:01:26,009
Planned purchases equal output, so stocks do not
change unexpectedly.

18
00:01:26,924 --> 00:01:31,325
Now planned investment rises by fifty million
pounds.

19
00:01:31,335 --> 00:01:36,009
At every income, planned expenditure is fifty
million higher.

20
00:01:36,019 --> 00:01:39,598
The whole line shifts upward, with the same
slope.

21
00:01:40,516 --> 00:01:46,772
At the old income of four hundred million,
buyers now plan to spend four hundred and fifty
million.

22
00:01:46,782 --> 00:01:51,690
Stocks fall unexpectedly, signalling that firms
should increase production.

23
00:01:52,596 --> 00:01:59,852
In this simplified round by round adjustment,
firms first raise output to four hundred and
fifty million pounds.

24
00:01:59,862 --> 00:02:04,559
The additional fifty million of output creates
fifty million of income.

25
00:02:05,468 --> 00:02:09,645
Households spend seventy five percent of the
extra income.

26
00:02:09,655 --> 00:02:14,474
Consumption rises by thirty seven point five
million pounds.

27
00:02:14,484 --> 00:02:19,760
Planned expenditure therefore reaches four
hundred and eighty seven point five million.

28
00:02:20,668 --> 00:02:23,213
Firms raise output again.

29
00:02:23,223 --> 00:02:29,200
The next income increase creates another twenty
eight point one two five million of consumption.

30
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:33,618
Each successive round is three quarters of the
previous round.

31
00:02:34,524 --> 00:02:38,753
The rounds continue, but saving makes each round
smaller.

32
00:02:38,763 --> 00:02:42,832
Income and planned expenditure approach the new
intersection.

33
00:02:42,842 --> 00:02:49,171
Induced consumption is movement along the new
expenditure line; it does not shift that line
again.

34
00:02:50,084 --> 00:02:54,090
The new equilibrium is six hundred million
pounds.

35
00:02:54,100 --> 00:03:00,208
Consumption is four hundred and fifty million,
and investment is one hundred and fifty million.

36
00:03:00,218 --> 00:03:03,876
Planned expenditure once again equals output.

37
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:10,325
The multiplier is one divided by one minus the
marginal propensity to consume.

38
00:03:10,335 --> 00:03:12,088
That gives four.

39
00:03:12,098 --> 00:03:18,862
Fifty million pounds of extra investment
therefore raises equilibrium income by two
hundred million pounds.

40
00:03:19,764 --> 00:03:22,257
Read the diagram carefully.

41
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:26,059
The vertical shift is fifty million pounds.

42
00:03:26,069 --> 00:03:30,612
The horizontal change in equilibrium income is
two hundred million.

43
00:03:30,622 --> 00:03:36,740
The total includes the initial investment plus
one hundred and fifty million of induced
consumption.
